\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf {Latent space of the SCP542 atlas under the two representations.} All 53{,}513{} cells of the 198{} cell lines, embedded by full-transcriptome PCA (left) and by scGPT (right), reduced to two dimensions by Uniform Manifold Approximation and Projection (UMAP) \cite {mcinnes2018umap} and coloured by cancer type. PCA separates the atlas into many compact islands, and a single colour recurs across several of them, so the islands are individual cell lines nested within lineage. scGPT projects the same cells onto one continuous manifold in which cancer type is only partly organised. The axes are UMAP coordinates and carry no units. The between-line share of variance that the figure shows qualitatively is quantified in Section~\ref {sec:results-q2} on the representations the models read, which differ from the plotted ones: PCA of the 5{,}000{} highly variable genes rather than of the full transcriptome, over the 153{} cross-validation lines rather than all 198{}. }}{8}{figure.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf {The pipeline in eight stages.} (1) One AUC per cell line and compound labels every cell of that line. The matrix marks screened (blue) and unscreened (grey) pairs. (2) The compound funnel from the 545{} CTRPv2 compounds through the 57{} FDA-approved ones to the 11{}-compound panel (the coverage stage between them is described in Section~\ref {sec:panel}). (3) The 28{} test lines are held out once. Five folds, grouped by cell line, cover the other 153{}. (4) The two representations, PCA (grey) and the frozen scGPT transformer (gold), both 512-dimensional. (5) The MLP with one output head per compound, shown with an example prediction per compound. (6) The masked objective, Equation~\ref {eq:objective}. (7) Evaluation: per-cell predictions are averaged per line and correlated with the measured AUC within each compound, shown for dasatinib. (8) Mean within-compound Spearman correlation of the unweighted MSE configuration of each arm and of the ridge control on each representation, over 11{} compounds and three seeds. The full comparison is in Table~\ref {tab:sweep}. }}{15}{figure.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf {The per-cell model.} One cell's 512-dimensional embedding (PCA or scGPT, never fine-tuned) passes through a shared trunk of two hidden blocks of 128{} and 64{} units, each a linear layer, layer normalisation, GELU and dropout 0.5{}, after input dropout 0.1{}, into 11{} linear heads, one per compound, which together form a single linear layer over the trunk. Right: the out-of-fold predicted AUC of one held-out line (SKES1, bone) per compound as bars, with the measured CTRPv2 value as diamonds. Low AUC means sensitive, high means resistant, and the bar shade follows the predicted value. Compounds are labelled by their CTRPv2 names. Platin (the CTRPv2 name for cisplatin) is the only one that differs from the common name. }}{19}{figure.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf {Per-compound score against label quality.} One point per panel compound ($n = 11$). Vertical axis: mean within-compound Spearman correlation, out of fold, of the highest-scoring configuration (PCA, MAE, $\alpha = 0.5$). Horizontal axis: share of the compound's CurveCurator fits that are flat, i.e.\ cannot reject a no-effect null ($p > 0.05$), on a logarithmic scale. Bold labels mark the highest (dasatinib) and lowest (cisplatin) scores and the exception to the trend (crizotinib). The inset reports the Spearman correlation over the eleven compounds. }}{24}{figure.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf {What cell-line identity alone predicts.} Mean within-compound Spearman correlation of two DrEval baselines under LPO evaluation, in which held-out (line, compound) pairs belong to lines seen in training: predicting each line's mean response (black, ``which cell line it is'') and each lineage's mean response (grey, ``lineage only''). Neither uses expression. Five folds of about 383 held-out pairs over the 11{} compounds; whiskers are the SD over folds. LPO scores are not comparable with the LCO scores of Table~\ref {tab:sweep}. }}{25}{figure.5}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf {Positive control of the heterogeneity criterion.} Distribution of the within-bag area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUROC) with which the MIL model separates the cells of two mixed cell lines whose response is known to differ, computed as the Mann--Whitney statistic divided by $n_A n_B$ \cite {mannwhitney1947,hanley1982}; one value per (compound, line pair, seed), $17{,}427$ per representation, shown as a density histogram for PCA (blue) and scGPT (gold). The dashed line marks chance (0.5); a value near 1 or 0 means the two populations are ranked apart. Medians: 0.518{} (PCA), 0.537{} (scGPT). }}{26}{figure.6}%
